# Line-ending normalization.
#
# Commit LF, check out LF — on every platform. This repo is developed on
# macOS/Linux (always LF) but is distributed downstream, including to
# Windows-clean white-label forks. Without this file, line endings are left
# to each contributor's `core.autocrlf` setting and to whatever bytes a tool
# writes (e.g. Python text-mode writers emit CRLF on Windows), so files drift
# to CRLF the moment Windows enters the picture. `eol=lf` pins both the
# committed blob and the working tree to LF, eliminating that drift at the
# source regardless of platform or git config.
#
# After adding/changing this file, run `git add --renormalize .` once to
# rewrite any already-committed CRLF (a no-op in an all-LF tree).

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never normalize.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Self-host projections — auto-resolve on merge, then regenerate.
#
# `packs/*/.apm/` and `packs/*/seeds/` are the source of truth; every path
# below is a pure function of them (agentbundle/build/self_host.py). A textual
# merge here settles nothing, because the only correct resolution is to re-run
# `make build-self`. The `regen` driver keeps one side so the merge does not
# halt; the self-host drift gate in `make build-check` then refuses a stale
# projection, so this defers regeneration and can never skip it.
#
# Register the driver once per clone: `make bootstrap-git`. Without it git
# reports `Unknown merge driver: regen` and falls back to a normal conflicting
# merge — degraded, never wrong.
#
# This list is not maintained by hand. It must equal the set of paths a
# required `gate-main` check covers, which tools/test_gitattributes_merge_driver.py
# measures by mutating a scratch tree and reading what the gate reports. Three
# paths look eligible and are not: `.codex/config.toml`, `tools/hooks/*.py`
# (`tools/**` is excluded from the drift comparison) and the repo-root
# `CLAUDE.md` symlink (git applies no content merge driver to a symlink blob).
# Placed at end of file: the `binary` macro above expands to `-merge`, and a
# later line wins.
.claude/**                                                merge=regen
.agents/**                                                merge=regen
.agentbundle/**                                           merge=regen
.claude-plugin/marketplace.json                           merge=regen
.codex/agents/**                                          merge=regen
.codex/hooks.json                                         merge=regen
/AGENT_RULES.md                                           merge=regen
docs/AGENTS.md                                            merge=regen
docs/CONVENTIONS.md                                       merge=regen
governance/manifest.example.yaml                          merge=regen
packages/agentbundle/agentbundle/_data/close_work.py      merge=regen
packages/agentbundle/agentbundle/_data/cooling.py         merge=regen
packages/agentbundle/agentbundle/_data/file_safety.py     merge=regen
packages/agentbundle/agentbundle/_data/work_intake_refresh.py    merge=regen
packages/agentbundle/agentbundle/_data/workspace_status_engine.py merge=regen
